WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.667
STEPHANIE WONG: This
week, we're talking

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.960
about better business
analytics, data warehousing,

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.542
and translation AI.

00:00:05.542 --> 00:00:07.500
Welcome to "This Week in
Cloud," where we serve

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.060
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.150
Google and Looker
are joining forces

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.180
to push cloud-based business
analytics even further.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.190
This means the addition
of several new features

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.140
to Google Cloud Platform,
including the power

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.630
to define metrics once
and then apply them

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.970
across data sets,
built-in applications

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:28.023
for industry-specific use cases,
and data visualization tools.

00:00:28.023 --> 00:00:29.940
Read more about what the
acquisition of Looker

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.520
means for GCP customers
on the Cloud blog.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.660
Then, try it out.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.720
But our roster
doesn't end there.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.630
We're also bringing Snowflake,
a leading cloud-based data

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.570
warehouse provider, into
the fold, in this case,

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.010
through our partnership.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.710
Customers who already use
Snowflake for powerful data

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:50.580
insights can now get seamless
access to GCP's AI tools

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.430
and, of course, our newly
reinforced data analytics

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:54.660
capabilities.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.520
See what a
partner-first strategy

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.640
looks like in practice on GCP.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.670
We at Google have been dealing
with translation for a while.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:06.540
So we're excited to announce
v3 of our Translation API.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.760
Listening to our customers,
we added new features

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.890
like choosing between
pre-trained and custom

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:14.370
models, batched translations,
and more granular control

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.670
over specific words and phrases.

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:19.260
Enjoy a smarter version of
the same powerful Translation

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.720
API without upgrading anything.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.850
Our treat.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.340
Knowing how to secure your
Kubernetes environment

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.230
is pretty important.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.360
The good news-- it's
never been easier

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.420
to learn how, thanks to our
self-paced lesson series

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.040
on Qwiklabs.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.990
Whether you're running
Kubernetes yourself

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.840
using our Google Kubernetes
Engine manage service

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.090
or using Anthos,
complete this quest

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.850
to learn the ins and outs
of migration, monitoring,

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:45.960
and security.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.567
Get started.

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:49.650
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:52.350
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.640
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.150
Leave us a comment, or tweet us.

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:57.680
We'll see you in the cloud.

